    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 48 tests pass, build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for `POST /api/owners`: an owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created and flagged.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the Owner schema (regenerated into `OwnerDto`): `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean` \u2014 wrapper, not primitive, so seed rows with NULL load cleanly) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) columns with accessors. MapStruct auto-maps them by name.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns. Tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required, not optional.\n\n4. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 new OfficeFloor function: scans existing owners; when the new owner shares a normalized `lastName` (case-insensitive, collapsed whitespace, matching the household-check convention) and an equal, present `postcode` while carrying a different telephone, it sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest matching owner's id; otherwise `false`/`null`. Runs before `save`, so it never matches itself.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignPossibleDuplicate` into the pipeline between `assignBulkSignupWarning` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance as the surrounding steps.\n\nThe new `Cp35Tests.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` passes, and the full suite (48 tests) stays green.",
